#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# is_array

#% text
# `is_array(x)` tests whether `x` is a full array: nested lists of equal lengths to some depth, with no list among the elements at that depth.

#% text
# `is_array(x, d)` also requires depth `d`; `is_array(x, d, test)` requires `test(e)` to be true for every element.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `d` may be an integer or a pattern the depth must match, such as `1 | 2` or `_`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
is_array([1, 2, 3, 4])
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_array([1, 2, [3], 4])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_array([[1, 2], [3, 4]], 2)
#% output
#= true

#% subsection
# Scope

#% cell
is_array([[1, 2], [3]])
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_array([[1, 2], [3, 4]], 1 | 2)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
is_array([[pi, e], [1, 2]], _, is_number)
#% output
#= false

#% cell
is_array([], 1)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `dimensions`, `array_depth`, `is_matrix`, `is_vector`
